    during P2" rulings 1 and 2, and "Planning verification and rulings on P1"
    ruling 2).
    
    Usage: lscmp.py <input archive> <output archive> [--diff <diff.tsv>] [--plant <flag>]
           lscmp.py <input archive> --parts
    
    Reads both archives with zipfile, byte spans and ElementTree, sharing no code
    with the library or the tool; its readers are M3 part 4 P1's gpcmp.py's,
    copied by line range (local, rels_of, workbook_of, w_of, top_level, qname,
    split_name, start_tag, opened, attributes, root_span, is_main, children,
    content_span, rels_prefix_of, bit3, cut, first_insert, et_first, values_of,
    with_attribute, without_attribute, merged, attr_value, col_retagged,
    bare_col, col_span, max_row, rows_of, apply, col_elements, et_cols, et_rows,
    covering). It finds W, the first <sheet> in <sheets> order whose
    relationship type is a worksheet's, and the styles part, the workbook's
    styles relationship's target; M, W's largest row number among its main <c>
    elements (a cell's r, else its row's r), 0 for none; i, the input's cellXfs
    <xf> count (the index add_style returns). From the input it builds the W the
    design gives (specs/0026 "The calls", P2 rulings 1 and 2; specs/0018's row
    creation and <col> split):
    
      row M + 1 carries s="i" then customFormat="1", each replaced between its
      quotes when the row's start tag has it, else appended after the last
      attribute; a present row keeps every other byte (ruling 1); an absent one
      is created as <row r="N" s="i" customFormat="1"/> with the <sheetData>'s
      prefix, before the first row numbered higher, else before </sheetData>;
      column 9 in <cols>: the covering <col> split so the column alone carries
      the edit (min and max replaced in place, the other pieces keeping every
      attribute), style="i" replaced or appended; an uncovered column given
      <col min="9" max="9" style="i"/> with the <cols>' prefix, placed by min;
      the pieces and the created element coalesced as P1 ruling 2 and P1
      verification ruling 2 say (whitespace alone between two pieces dropped
      when they merge), an element the edit did not touch kept as it is; <cols>
      created before the first main root child the 39-name table puts after it
      when W has none.
    
    Of the styles part it checks the spec's three facts, with no design bytes:
    cellXfs one longer, the input's content a byte-identical prefix, its count
    attribute (when present) the new count, the new <xf>'s fontId the input's
    font count; fonts one longer, the input's content a byte-identical prefix,
    its count attribute the new count, the new <font> holding one main <b>;
    every byte outside <fonts> and <cellXfs> the input's.
    
    It compares:
    
      rest_same    W with every main <cols> and <sheetData> cut out is the
                   input's W with its own cut out, byte for byte
      places       W's main root children's names are the input's with a
                   created <cols> where the table puts it
      schema_order W's main root children are in the table's order, one each of
                   <cols> and <sheetData>
      rows_kept    <sheetData> with row M + 1 cut out is the input's with its own
                   row M + 1 cut out, byte for byte
      row_window   the output's row M + 1 is the design's, byte for byte (present
                   edited in place, absent created; ruling 1)
      row_attrs    read with ElementTree, row M + 1 carries exactly the input
                   row's attributes (r alone for one the input lacks) with s and
                   customFormat set, and a created row has no child
      cols_other   the output's <col> elements outside the span the edit covers
                   (column 9 and the input <col> covering it) are the input's
                   outside it, byte for byte, in order
      cols_split   read with ElementTree, the output's <col> elements inside that
                   span cover it exactly, in order; the one over column 9 covers
                   it alone and carries style="i"; every element keeps its
                   source's attributes but min and max (and style on column 9's)
      cols_bytes   the output's <cols> is the design's, byte for byte
      w_bytes      W is exactly the W the design gives
      styles_xfs   cellXfs as above
      styles_fonts fonts as above
      styles_rest  the styles part with <fonts> and <cellXfs> cut out is the
                   input's with its own cut out, byte for byte
      others_same  every entry but W and the styles part is the input's, byte
                   for byte, the names the input's in the input's order
      read_back    read with ElementTree, the tool's figures: row M + 1 carries
                   s="i" and customFormat="1"; one <col> covers column 9, alone,
                   with style="i"; cellXfs one longer
      xml_values   with --diff, the runner's diff.<label>.tsv for the pair: its
                   xml "values" rows are W's and the styles part's alone, W's
                   in_only and out_only the one-sided counts of the input's
