    It prints ONE line of counts and yes/no flags and no text, reference, sheet
    name or part name: the line's counts beside the tool's (rows, present rows,
    cols, col_split, kept_cols, xfs), the shapes (case: 1 when no input <col>
    covers column 9, 0 when the covering one is split, 2 when it covers column 9
    alone; created_cols, created_rows, edited_rows). --parts prints W's part
    name and 1, 0 or - for its bit 3, then the styles part's name and its bit 3,
    one per line, for the log to compare with the runner's rows without
